h1('17. Glossary')
tb([['Term','Meaning'],['AUC','Take one funded and one failed campaign. AUC is how often the model gives the funded one the higher score. 0.5 = guessing, 1 = perfect'],['AUC within category','The same, but both campaigns come from the same category; averaged by size over the categories that have both outcomes (163 in 2025)'],['Accuracy','Share of campaigns for which "funded" or "failed" was predicted correctly'],['Baseline','A trivial rule to beat, for example "always funded"'],['Calibration','Making the predicted percentage match what really happened (70% should mean about 70 in 100)'],['Leakage','Using information that would not be known at decision time; it makes a model look better than it is'],['Selection bias','The data is not a fair sample: here, failed campaigns are under-represented'],['XGBoost','Many small decision trees built one after another, each correcting the errors of the previous ones'],['TF-IDF','Turns a text into numbers: one weight per word, higher for words that are frequent in this text and rare elsewhere'],['SHAP','Splits a prediction into the contribution of each input'],['Odds','Chance divided by (1 − chance). 80% is odds of 4 to 1'],['Cohort','The group of teams a coach looks after'],['Capped category','One of the 29 categories where the public listing limit is reached']],[38,132])

